==History==
2022
*The Super Witch [[Cards|card]] was made available in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Super Witch Challenge]] on 13/5/2022.
*On 22/5/2022, the Super Witch was removed from the game.
2023
*On 31/7/2023, the Super Witch was readded to the game in the Super Witch Event.
*On 8/8/2023, the Super Witch was removed from the game.
2024
*On 19/8/2024, the Super Witch was readded to the game in the Super Cards Draft Event.
*On 26/8/2024, the Super Witch was removed from the game.
2025
*On 27/1/2025, the Super Witch was readded to the game in the Super Cards Draft Event.
*On 3/2/2025, the Super Witch was removed from the game.
*On 19/5/2025, the Super Witch was readded to the game in the Hexed Havoc Event.
*On 26/5/2025, the Super Witch was removed from the game.
*On 6/10/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/10/2025)=|Balance Update]] increased the Skeleton's attack time interval to 1.1 seconds (from 1.0 seconds).

==Trivia==
*The Super Witch is shown to make the practice of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Necromancy necromancy]. Necromancy is a form of magic involving communication with the deceased; either by summoning their spirit as an apparition or raising them bodily.
**In the Japanese language setting of the game, the Super Witch's name translates to "Super Necromancer". In the Malaysian language setting of the game, the Super Witch's name translates to "Super Magic Girl".
*The [[Bats]] that the Super Witch spawns resemble the in-life bat species called "''Desmodus rotundus"'' ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_vampire_bat common vampire bat]). The common vampire bat is a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hematophagy hematophagous] bat species that primarily feeds on the blood of livestock, which is done by biting their prey while they are sleeping. In Clash Royale, Bats attack in a similar way by biting their enemies.
*The Super Witch is a reference to the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Super_Witch eponymous troop] in Clash of Clans. 
**However, the Super Witch in Clash Royale alternates between spawning [[Skeletons]] and [[Bats]], instead of spawning [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Super_Witch/Big_Boy Big Boys].
**Unlike in Clash of Clans, the Super Witch in Clash Royale shares an identical design with the [[Witch]].
*The Super Witch is 1 of 15 [[cards]] associated with Skeletons, with the others being [[Bomber]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Tombstone]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Guards]], [[Skeleton Army]], Witch, [[Balloon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Graveyard]], [[Skeleton King]], and of course, Skeletons. 
**It is the only Skeleton-related card to be released as a temporary card.
*The Super Witch's card image is indentical to the [[Witch/Merge Tactics|Witch's Merge Tactics counterpart]]'s card image.
*It is rumored that the Super Witch has been summoned from all the other 3 Witches, as demonstrated in the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VQf90EQVeX8 Super Witch trailer], hence explaining the combination of all the other Witches' abilities.
*The Super Witch is the subject of a [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] item.
**The Super Witch is one of the first troops to be the subject of a Battle Banner item, along with the [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], Giant Skeleton, [[Mega Knight]], and the [[Golden Knight]].

